---
import LegalSections from "../components/LegalSections.astro";
import PageHero from "../components/PageHero.astro";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

const updated = "September 19, 2026";
const sections = [
  {
    title: "Who we are",
    points: [
      "Vectis is built by Dániel Kerekes (kerd.dev), who is responsible for the hosted service at vectis.kerd.dev. Contact: kerd@kerd.dev.",
      "This policy covers the website and the hosted account service. The Vectis app, CLI and service run on your own Mac and send nothing to us unless you connect that Mac to an account.",
    ],
  },
  {
    title: "What stays on your Mac",
    points: [
      "VM images and disks, build files, service logs, and local credentials never leave your machine. Machine and controller credentials are kept in the macOS Keychain.",
      "Jobs talk to GitHub directly. Logs, artifacts and caches your workflows upload go to GitHub under GitHub's terms.",
    ],
  },
  {
    title: "What the account service stores",
    points: [
      "Your sign-in account, handled by Clerk: email address, sign-in method, and an account ID.",
      "Linked GitHub identities: GitHub user ID, login, and the App installations you can access. GitHub user tokens are used only during verification and are not saved.",
      "Machines you connect: name, a local ID, environment summaries such as OS, CPU and memory, last-seen time, and fingerprints of their credentials.",
      "Repository connections, GitHub job states and labels, runner leases, and the status and results of operations you submit.",
      "Workflow files read for a migration preview, kept for 24 hours. Answers to remote queries, kept for about a minute. Single-use runner configurations, deleted within 15 minutes.",
    ],
  },
  {
    title: "Why we use it",
    points: [
      "Only to provide the service you asked for: signing in, connecting Macs and repositories, starting runners for your jobs, and remote control. The legal basis is performing our agreement with you.",
      "We do not sell data, show ads, or use analytics or tracking cookies. The website stores your theme choice in your browser; Clerk sets the cookies it needs to keep you signed in.",
    ],
  },
  {
    title: "Who processes it",
    points: [
      "Clerk (authentication), Convex (backend and database), and Cloudflare (website hosting and network) process data on our behalf. GitHub receives the requests needed to register runners and read job states for the repositories you connect.",
      "These providers may process data outside the European Union under their own safeguards, such as standard contractual clauses.",
    ],
  },
  {
    title: "How long we keep it",
    points: [
      "Account, machine and repository data is kept while your account exists. Disconnected repositories and revoked machines stop being used immediately.",
      "To delete your account and its data, email kerd@kerd.dev from the address you sign in with. We delete it within 30 days.",
    ],
  },
  {
    title: "Your rights",
    points: [
      "You can ask to access, correct, export or delete your data, or object to how it is used. You can also complain to your data protection authority; in Hungary that is the NAIH.",
      "We will post changes to this policy on this page and update the date below.",
      `Last updated ${updated}.`,
    ],
  },
];
---

<Base title="Privacy" description="What the Vectis account service stores, why, and for how long.">
  <PageHero title="Privacy">
    <p>Vectis keeps your CI on your Mac. The account service stores only what it needs to connect your Macs to GitHub.</p>
  </PageHero>
  <LegalSections sections={sections} />
</Base>
